## Context

Child of tracking ticket 0252 (model A, ratified 2026-07-13). Incident I1
(aedist, 2026-06-11/12): a session's worktree was deregistered mid-session;
the directory remained, so bare git commands fell through to the PRIMARY
repo and a `git checkout -B` moved the primary checkout off main. Every
existing guard checks the weak predicate ("cwd is some worktree") and let
it through. Full audit: docs/audit-0252-worktree-ownership-2026-07-12.md.

## Relevant files

- `scripts/guard-cd-primary-repo.sh` — closest existing guard; pattern to follow for hook JSON handling
- `scripts/pretooluse-worktree-path-guard.sh` — sibling PreToolUse guard, advisory
- `~/.claude/settings.json` — hook registration (PreToolUse, Bash matcher)

## Actions

1. New PreToolUse guard on Bash commands that mutate git/erg state
   (commit, checkout, switch, merge, rebase, push, reset, erg close/new/log).
2. Fast-path: if cwd does not contain `/.claude/worktrees/`, exit 0
   (primary-checkout work is governed by other guards).
3. Otherwise compare the cwd worktree-name segment against
   `basename $(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)`; block with an explanatory
   message on mismatch or when rev-parse resolves to the primary root.
4. Whitelist explicit `git -C <path>` invocations — that idiom is the
   sanctioned way to intentionally mutate another tree.
5. Register the hook; keep total overhead at one rev-parse (~5-20 ms).

## Test

- Red first: simulate I1 — a cwd under `.claude/worktrees/<name>/` whose
  `git rev-parse --show-toplevel` resolves to the primary root — and assert
  the guard blocks a `git commit` there.

## Verification

- [ ] Guard blocks mutation when rev-parse resolves outside the cwd worktree
- [ ] Guard passes normal in-worktree mutation (no false positives in a raid wave)
- [ ] `git -C` invocations pass through
- [ ] Read-only git (status, log, diff) is never blocked

## Invariants

- `make check` passes; existing guards unaffected
- Guard stays cheap enough to run on every Bash call (single rev-parse)

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Guard script + hook registration merged
- [ ] Tests cover I1 replay, false-positive path, and the `git -C` whitelist
- [ ] `make check` passes
